<title>SWEDEN: Sweden reduces six-month t-bill issue volume.</title>
<headline>Sweden reduces six-month t-bill issue volume.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's national debt office said on Wednesday it reduced the issue volume of six-month T-bills from five billion to 1.9 billion at the weekly auction.</p>
<p>					    176 day bill    322 day bill</p>
<p> Volume issued (billion Skr)	  1.898	     4.997</p>
<p> Total bids (billion Skr)	     2.498	     6.640</p>
<p> Number of accepted bids		   19		  33</p>
<p> Number of bids				22		  41</p>
<p> Lowest rate				4.230	     4.415</p>
<p> Highest accepted rate		  4.250	     4.440</p>
<p> Weighted average rate		  4.244	     4.430</p>
<p> Percent served at highest rate	 100	     54.62</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1017</p>
</text>
